# zngl-viewer-sample License

Copyright (c) 2026 haidi-ai (ZNGL project)
<https://github.com/haidi-ai/zngl-viewer-sample>

This repository contains sample viewer pages that call the ZNGL low-level
API. **It does not contain ZNGL itself.**

## 1. Sample code — MIT License

The MIT License text at the bottom of this file applies **only** to the sample
code authored in this repository:

- `01-hello.html`, `02-pick.html`, `03-hiddenline.html` (their HTML, CSS and
  JavaScript), and
- any future sample code files added to this repository.

## 2. What the MIT grant does NOT cover

- **`dist/` and the ZNGL runtime.** `dist/zngl.js` is not distributed in this
  repository (it is `.gitignore`d). It is **not** licensed by this file; get it
  from the official ZNGL release package and use it under ZNGL's own license /
  EULA terms.
- **The ZNGL engine, license-check logic, license files and signing material.**
  None are present here, and none are licensed by this file.
- **The ZNKernel-II kernel.** Not present; not licensed here.
- **Screenshots** under `screenshots/`: copyright (c) 2026 haidi-ai (ZNGL
  project), all rights reserved (included to document these samples).
- **Documentation text** (`README.md`, `LICENSE-NOTICE.md`, this file): provided
  for reference; link to it or quote short excerpts with attribution, but do
  not republish it wholesale without permission.
- **Trademarks.** "ZNGL", "ZNKernel-II" and associated logos are marks of their
  owner; MIT does not grant trademark rights.

`LICENSE-NOTICE.md` remains in force as the explanation of ZNGL's licensing
tiers (low-level API free, Engine commercial). It is **not** replaced by this
file. If this file and `LICENSE-NOTICE.md` conflict on any ZNGL material, the
official ZNGL terms prevail.

